      "message": "Really what matters here is the final Metal swizzle, not the frontend swizzle. Technically I think the current code has the correct outcome (it\u0027s just pessimistic for depth/stencil textures), but that\u0027s hard to tell since there\u0027s non-trivial logic to determine the actual Metal swizzle later.\n\nDoing it up front would be more direct, something like this:\n\n```\nstd::optional\u003cMTLTextureSwizzleChannels\u003e mtlSwizzle;\nif (SupportTextureComponentSwizzle(...)) {\n  wgpu::TextureComponentSwizzle swizzle \u003d // ... compute the swizzle...\n  if (UsesNonDefaultSwizzle(swizzle)) {\n    mtlSwizzle \u003d ToMetalTextureSwizzle(swizzle);\n  }\n} else {\n  DAWN_ASSERT(!UsesNonDefaultSwizzle(texture, swizzle));\n}\nbool needsNewView \u003d ...; // now simply just checks mtlSwizzle.has_value()\n\n// ...\n\nif (mtlSwizzle) {\n  mtlTextureView \u003d ...;\n} else {\n  mtlTextureView \u003d ...;\n}\n```\n\nSorry for a slightly structural late comment. Should be a pretty small change overall though.",
